    <td>R31.0</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem echoing his documented urinary complaints and last illness; superseded by the diagnosis at the third chronic-care visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Chronic urinary retention with overflow (post-void residual 460 mL at intake), worsened by a nightly anticholinergic sleep aid; drained by an indwelling catheter</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R33.8</td><td>S — Synthetic finding echoing the strangury and catheterization documented in his last weeks.</td>
  </tr>
